# {{.Title}}

Created with `gortisan create`. Every file here belongs to this project: nothing
imports gortisan, and gortisan is not in `go.mod`. Change anything.

## Run

```bash
cp .env.example .env
./gortisan run               # builds, runs, and restarts on every change
                             # (or: go run ./cmd/{{.Name}})
curl localhost:8080/ping     # {"ping":"pong"}
curl localhost:8080/health   # {"status":"pass","checks":{...}}
{{- if .Metrics}}
curl localhost:8080/metrics  # Prometheus; set METRICS_SECRET to require a bearer token
{{- end}}
```
{{- if .Kafka}}

Workers run in their own process: `./gortisan run worker -- <feature>.<name>` or
`go run ./cmd/worker <feature>.<name>`.
{{- end}}

## Layout

The layout the Go team recommends for servers
([go.dev/doc/modules/layout](https://go.dev/doc/modules/layout#server-project)):
commands in `cmd/`, the rest in `internal/`. Each subject is one package with
focused files, not one package per layer:

```
cmd/{{.Name}}/main.go       builds every dependency in order and starts the server
internal/
  user/                 one package per subject (make:model user, make:handler user/list…)
    user.go             the struct — the table
    repository.go       reads and writes the table; its mapping is generated at the end
    service.go          business logic
    handler.go          HTTP endpoints
    request.go          inputs, with Validate
    response.go         outputs
  config/               environment variables (and .env) → Config
  server/               echo: request log, panic recovery, JSON errors, graceful shutdown
  router/               every route, in one file
  health/               /ping and /health
  validate/             field errors → one 422
{{- if .Postgres}}
  database/             the PostgreSQL pool, DBTX and InTx
  database/orm/         a small mapper from structs to tables (optional)
{{- end}}
{{- if .Redis}}
  cache/                the Redis client
{{- end}}
{{- if .Kafka}}
  kafka/                Kafka readers, writers and Publish
{{- end}}
{{- if .Metrics}}
  metrics/              Prometheus metrics and /metrics
{{- end}}
{{- if .Postgres}}
migrations/             SQL migrations, *.up.sql / *.down.sql
{{- end}}
```

## Rules

- **Dependencies are passed, not looked up.** Constructors take what they need;
  `main.go` wires them. No globals, no values hidden in `context.Context`.
- **Errors carry the status.** A handler returns `echo.NewHTTPError(code, "message")`
  for a client error; any other error becomes a 500 and is logged.
- **Validation returns every error at once.** `var errs validate.Errors`, then
  `errs.Add(...)` / `errs.Check(ctx, field, rule)`, then `return errs.Err()`.
{{- if .Postgres}}
- **Transactions are explicit.** `database.InTx(ctx, db, func(tx pgx.Tx) error { ... })`
  and `repo.WithTx(tx)`.

## The database layer

A model is a struct marked `//gortisan:table <name>`; every field with a `db` tag
is a column (`db:"id,pk"` for the primary key, `db:"created_at,default"` for a
column the database fills). Its mapping is generated into the end of the
package's `repository.go`, between `// gortisan:table <Type> begin` and `end` —
by `make:model`, by `./gortisan run` on every save, or by `./gortisan generate`.
To add a column, add a field and a migration. Nothing reads the tags at run
time. Using the mapper is optional:

```go
// with the mapper
u, err := userTable.Find(ctx, r.db, id)
users, err := userTable.Get(ctx, r.db, orm.Where("mobile LIKE ?", "0912%").OrderBy("id DESC").Limit(20))

// plain SQL, same connection or transaction
var n int64
err := r.db.QueryRow(ctx, `SELECT count(*) FROM users WHERE created_at >= $1`, since).Scan(&n)
```

To drop the mapper, rewrite the repository methods with SQL and delete
`internal/database/orm`.
{{- end}}

## Generate more

`./gortisan` (`gortisan.bat` or `.\gortisan.ps1` on Windows) runs the gortisan
version this project was created with, through `go run`. It is not a dependency:
no code imports it and `go.mod` does not list it. Delete the three scripts if you
do not want them.

```bash
./gortisan list                                   # every command and flag
{{- if .Postgres}}
./gortisan make:model user                        # internal/user: user.go, repository.go + a migration
./gortisan make:migration add_index_to_users
{{- end}}
./gortisan make:service user                      # internal/user/service.go
./gortisan make:handler user/list                 # handler.go + ListRequest + ListResponse
./gortisan make:enum user/status --members "active,blocked"
./gortisan make:validator user/mobile_free
./gortisan make:middleware request_id
./gortisan make:client payment
{{- if .Redis}}
./gortisan make:cache user/profile --type "*User"
{{- end}}
{{- if .Kafka}}
./gortisan make:worker user/send_welcome --topic users.created
{{- if .Postgres}}
./gortisan make:cdc user
{{- end}}
{{- end}}
```
